# AWS-managed SSE-S3 is an explicit cost constraint for both private buckets.
AVD-AWS-0132
# SNS uses alias/aws/sns to avoid a dedicated customer-managed KMS key charge.
AVD-AWS-0136
# The adopted root volume retains its live encryption state; an unencrypted
# volume follows the separately approved snapshot/copy replacement runbook.
AVD-AWS-0131
# The RDS instance deliberately follows the same cost constraint. It contains
# no customer-managed encryption key and replacement uses snapshots only.
# RDS storage encryption is deliberately disabled as a cost constraint.
AVD-AWS-0080
# Discord, Supabase, Docker Hub and AWS public APIs require internet egress;
# the instance deliberately has zero ingress and no NAT/private-endpoint scope.
AVD-AWS-0104
